Subject: Stop clearing the source register of a transfer move in its step form

What this does
  Under deferred reference counting the step form of `move_xfer` copies its
  source to its destination and leaves the source as it was, the same as the
  interpreter loop and the threaded handler.

Why we need it
  `0279` removed the clear from the interpreter loop and the threaded handler
  but not from the generated step form, so an instruction run one at a time
  (compiled code's op call) wrote a register the other two executors leave
  alone. The result was the same because the source is dead, but compiled code
  relies on a handler writing only the registers its format declares, and its
  register-write check reported this one at every transfer move.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.

diff --git a/quickjs-regvm-step.inc b/quickjs-regvm-step.inc
--- a/quickjs-regvm-step.inc
+++ b/quickjs-regvm-step.inc
@@ -4081,7 +4081,6 @@
                   if (d != s) {
 #if QJS_DRC
                       regs[d] = regs[s];
-                      regs[s] = JS_UNDEFINED;
 #else
                       set_value(ctx, &regs[d], regs[s]);
                       regs[s] = JS_UNDEFINED;
